         Voting in Acton Voter registration must be completed by the deadline in order to vote in a given election. The last day to register to vote for any election held will be 10 days prior to the election.  Click here to register:  https://www.sec.state.ma.us/OVR/ The Residents of Acton have at least two opportunities to vote for  local  offices and issues each year, the Annual Town Election & the Annual Town Meeting. If an  additional  Special Town Election or Special Town Meeting is being called, residents will be notified once the date is set. The  State  Election calendar can be found  here . Voter registration must be completed by the deadline in order to vote in a given election. The Annual Town Election is held on the Tuesday immediately preceding the first Monday in May of each year, this year it will be  APRIL 27, 2027 . During this election, voters may either vote by mail in ballot after submitting a mail in  ballot application  or vote at their designated polling location. The Town is divided geographically into 8 precincts.  Click here  for help finding your precinct. The  Annual Town Meeting  is held on the first Monday in May of each year, this year it will be  May 3, 2027  . The Town issues a Warrant which contains all of the items being voted on. If all of the items in the Warrant are not covered on the first night, the Town Meeting will continue onto additional consecutive nights. Participants must be present in order to vote in this Parliamentary-style election. All precincts attend Town Meetings at the Acton-Boxborough Regional High School,  36 Charter Rd .  Elected Officials Some of the  Boards and Committees  in Acton are elected directly by the residents of Acton. Others are appointed by the Select Board, Town Moderator, or Town Manager. Offices filled by vote at the Annual Town Election or by Special Election as required are: Select Board  - 5 Members, 3 Year Terms Town Moderator  - 1 Year Term Acton-Boxborough Regional School Committee  - 7 of 11 Members from Acton, 3 Year Terms Acton Housing Authority  - 3 Elected Members, 1 State Appointed, 5 Year Terms Acton Water District  - 3 Year Terms Trustees of the Acton Memorial Library  - 3 Members, 6 Corporate Members, 3 Year Terms Offices elected by vote at the Annual Town Meeting include: Assistant Town Moderator - 1 Year Term Trustees of the Acton Firefighters Relief Fund - 3 Members, 3 Year Terms Trustees of the Charlotte Goodnow Fund - 3 Members, 3 Year Terms Trustees of the Elizabeth White Fund - 3 Members, 3 Year Terms Trustees of the West Acton Citizens’ Library - 3 Members, 3 Year Terms Past Town Elections and Reports Town Election Results Most Recent Results  |  View All Town Meeting & Special Town Meeting Abstracts Most Recent Results  |  View All State Election Results Most Recent Results  |  View All Annual Town Reports Most Recent Results  |  View All Additional Resources Massachusetts Elections Division Town Charter Town By-Laws Precinct Map   
     

 
